  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Futures: Protection and Education for Children and Youth in Northeast Syria - Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;overall objective &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;of the project is to increase the resilience and well-being of vulnerable children, youth and caregivers in three governorates of North East Syria (NES)- Deir-ez-Zor, Ar-Raqqa and Al-Hasakeh- through the provision of quality education, psychosocial and livelihoods support and child protection services, accompanied by efforts to promote the rights and well-being of children in detention and/or associated with armed groups.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The Action will have four specific objectives/outcomes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;focused on protection, social cohesion &amp; resilience, education, and support to CAAFAG. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The proposed integrated approach will provide a comprehensive response to vulnerable children and their families, thus reducing the risk of radicalisation and recruitment by armed groups, as well as supporting meaningful reintegration. The four specific objectives/outcomes the Action will achieve are as follows: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;1. To protect vulnerable children in NES from violence, exploitation, abuse and neglect;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;2. To improve the resilience of vulnerable children, youth and their caregivers in NES and increase community-level social cohesion; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;3. To improve access to education in safe learning spaces for vulnerable children in NES;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;4. To protect Children Associated with Armed Forces and Armed Groups (CAAFAG) from further harm, improve their well-being and have viable pathways for reintegration or repatriation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
